From 189c39db6e24e5a7ca13fc18ff5d85009a3cbdd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: darshp848 <75503951+darshp848@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:57:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Validate the match decision tree on 300-second runs

Add a deterministic decision matrix over the shipped v4 plan and an opt-in
five-minute wall-clock run against the local station HTTP API. The matrix
found three gaps, fixed here:

- a match reset now gets its full settle time plus a verification window
  before it can time out
- after an unverified reset, only another reset may follow (no plain retry)
- a stop acknowledged at or after the 300 s deadline no longer counts as an
  on-time finish (runner and CLI stop cue)

The plug stage budget rises to 30 s to fit a verified reset. The wall-clock
test accepts an early stop when under one verification check remains.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
